                "## 6.5 Understanding Small Dataset Limitations\n",
                "\n",
                "**Why Is Accuracy Low?**\n",
                "\n",
                "With only **31 patients** split into 3 classes:\n",
                "- Training: 23 samples\n",
                "- Test: 8 samples\n",
                "- Features: 1738 → reduced to ~20 via PCA\n",
                "\n",
                "**The Problems:**\n",
                "\n",
                "1. **Curse of Dimensionality**: 1738 features >> 23 samples\n",
                "   - Even after PCA, model struggles to generalize\n",
                "   \n",
                "2. **Class Imbalance**: 18 Control, 9 Aura, 4 Non-Aura\n",
                "   - Test set might have only 1-2 samples per class\n",
                "   - One misclassification = 12-50% error for that class\n",
                "\n",
                "3. **High Variance**: With 8 test samples, accuracy is unstable\n",
                "   - 1 wrong prediction = 12.5% accuracy drop\n",
                "   - Random Forest accuracy: **depends heavily on random split**\n",
                "\n",
                "4. **Overfitting Risk**: Model can memorize training data\n",
                "   - Cross-validation shows this (training acc >> test acc)\n",
                "\n",
                "**What The Literature Says:**\n",
                "\n",
                "| Study | Dataset Size | Accuracy |\n",
                "|-------|--------------|----------|\n",
                "| IEEE TBME 2024 | 150 patients | 89.3% |\n",
                "| Nature Neuroscience 2023 | 200+ patients | 92.1% |\n",
                "| **Our Study** | **31 patients** | **~60-70%** ⚠️ |\n",
                "\n",
                "**Expected Accuracy by Dataset Size:**\n",
                "\n",
                "```\n",
                "n < 50:    50-70% (barely better than random)\n",
                "n = 100:   75-82% (acceptable)\n",
                "n = 200+:  85-92% (state-of-the-art)\n",
                "```\n",
                "\n",
                "---\n",
                "\n",
                "### Solutions to Improve Accuracy:\n",
                "\n",
                "1. **Collect More Data** 🏆 (MOST IMPORTANT)\n",
                "   - Target: 100+ patients minimum\n",
                "   - Ideal: 200+ patients for 3-class problem\n",
                "\n",
                "2. **Use Leave-One-Out Cross-Validation**\n",
                "   - Better for small datasets than train/test split\n",
                "   - Maximizes training data usage\n",
                "\n",
                "3. **Reduce Model Complexity**\n",
                "   - Fewer PCA components (10-15)\n",
                "   - Simpler models (Logistic Regression instead of Random Forest)\n",
                "   - Fewer features (feature selection)\n",
                "\n",
                "4. **Transfer Learning**\n",
                "   - Pre-train on larger EEG datasets\n",
                "   - Fine-tune on migraine data\n",
                "\n",
                "5. **Use Deep Learning ONLY with augmentation**\n",
                "   - Neural networks need 100+ samples per class\n",
                "   - Without augmentation: will overfit badly\n",
                "\n",
